---
import Legal from "../layouts/Legal.astro";
import { legalAddress, legalCompany, legalMailto } from "../lib/legal";
---

<Legal
  title="Legal notice — Zenguy"
  description="Legal notice (aviso legal) of NIESAYO GROUP, S.L., the provider of Zenguy, under Spanish LSSI-CE."
  eyebrow="Aviso legal"
  heading="Legal notice"
>
  <p>
    This legal notice identifies the provider of the information-society services
    available at {legalCompany.site} and {legalCompany.app} (together, the
    “websites”), as required by article 10 of Law 34/2002 of 11 July on
    information-society services and electronic commerce (LSSI-CE).
  </p>

  <h2>1. Service provider</h2>
  <dl>
    <dt>Legal name</dt>
    <dd>{legalCompany.legalName}</dd>
    <dt>Trade name</dt>
    <dd>{legalCompany.tradeName}</dd>
    <dt>Tax ID (NIF)</dt>
    <dd>{legalCompany.nif}</dd>
    <dt>Registered office</dt>
    <dd>{legalAddress}</dd>
    <dt>Companies register</dt>
    <dd>{legalCompany.registry}</dd>
    <dt>Email</dt>
    <dd><a href={legalMailto}>{legalCompany.email}</a></dd>
    <dt>Websites</dt>
    <dd>
      <a href={legalCompany.site}>{legalCompany.site}</a>
      {" "}and{" "}
      <a href={legalCompany.app}>{legalCompany.app}</a>
    </dd>
  </dl>
  <p>
    Zenguy is a trade name of {legalCompany.legalName}. Email is the ordinary
    channel for a direct and effective communication with the provider, as
    article 10.1.c LSSI-CE requires.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Purpose of the websites</h2>
  <p>
    The websites describe and provide access to Zenguy, a software service that
    runs natural-language browser tests and HTTP uptime checks on sites the
    customer authorises. Use of the application itself is also governed by the
    {" "}
    <a href="/terms/">Terms of Service</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Users and conditions of use</h2>
  <p>
    Anyone who accesses the websites is a user. Access is free of charge aside
    from the user’s own network costs. Using the websites implies that the user
    has read this notice, the{" "}
    <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> and the{" "}
    <a href="/cookies/">Cookie Policy</a>. Paid use of Zenguy also requires
    acceptance of the Terms of Service at registration.
  </p>
  <p>
    The user must use the websites lawfully, in good faith, and without damaging
    the provider, other users, or third parties. In particular the user must not
    introduce malware, attempt unauthorised access, overload the service, scrape
    it in a way that impairs it, or use it to test systems they do not own or
    are not authorised to test.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Intellectual and industrial property</h2>
  <p>
    The websites, their design, software, trademarks, copy and other contents
    belong to {legalCompany.legalName} or to their licensors. Viewing them does
    not transfer any rights. Reproduction, distribution, public communication or
    transformation of those contents beyond private, personal use requires prior
    written permission, except where a mandatory limitation of Spanish
    intellectual-property law applies.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Liability</h2>
  <p>
    The provider makes reasonable efforts to keep the websites available and
    free of harmful code, but does not warrant uninterrupted access, the
    absence of errors, or the fitness of the public marketing pages for any
    particular purpose. The application’s contractual warranties and limits
    are those set out in the Terms of Service, without prejudice to mandatory
    rights of consumers and users under Royal Legislative Decree 1/2007
    (TRLGDCU).
  </p>
  <p>
    The provider is not responsible for third-party websites linked from these
    pages, nor for the user’s use of those sites. Linking does not imply
    endorsement.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Prices and contracting</h2>
  <p>
    Subscription prices, included usage, taxes and the billing cycle are shown
    in the application before payment and in Stripe Checkout. Marketing pages
    may display a reference price; the price that binds the parties is the one
    confirmed at checkout, including applicable VAT or equivalent tax.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Personal data</h2>
  <p>
    Personal data are processed as described in the{" "}
    <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>, under Regulation (EU) 2016/679
    (GDPR) and Organic Law 3/2018 (LOPDGDD).
  </p>

  <h2>8. Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    Information about cookies and similar technologies is in the{" "}
    <a href="/cookies/">Cookie Policy</a>, under article 22.2 LSSI-CE and the
    AEPD cookie guidance.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Applicable law and venue</h2>
  <p>
    This notice is governed by the laws of Spain. Unless a mandatory rule
    (including consumer law) gives the user a different venue, the courts of
    Barcelona, Spain have jurisdiction over disputes about the public websites.
    Disputes about the paid service follow the Terms of Service.
  </p>
</Legal>
